hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3054","###\n Muhammad ibn Bashshar narrated to us, saying: Hammad, meaning Ibn Mas'adah, narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dh'ib narrated to us, on the authority of 'Ata', on the authority of 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from Ibn 'Abbas (RA), who said: \"In the early days of Hajj, people used to conduct trade in Mina, 'Arafah, the market of Dhul-Majaz, and during the Hajj seasons. They feared that"
"3055","**\nNarrated to us Bundār, narrated to us Abū Bakr al-Ḥanafiyy, narrated to us Ibn Abī Dhī’b with this chain in a similar narration.\n\nAnd narrated to us Aḥmad ibn ʿAbdah, informed us Ḥammād ibn Zayd, from ʿUbayd Allāh ibn Abī Yazīd, who said: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr reciting this verse:\n*\"There is no blame upon you for seeking bounty from your Lord\"* [Qur’an 2:198]\nduring the seasons of Hajj."
